    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `fill_gaps` in `app/gaps.py`, and all 4 tests pass: the 2 that were already there and 2 new ones I added.\n\n**How it works:**\n- It works on a copy of the input, so the frame you pass in is never changed.\n- Each missing `temp_c` is filled from the same station only: first with its most recent earlier reading, then, if there is none, with its first later one.\n- Only missing values are replaced. Existing temperatures and the other columns stay the same, and the row order and index are kept, even if the index has repeated labels.\n- A station with no temperatures at all keeps its missing values.\n- Rows with no station ID are left alone. They aren't filled, and their temperatures aren't used for any other station. This case wasn't in your spec, so I treated a missing ID as an unknown station rather than a real one.\n\n**Tests:** I wasn't allowed to run inline Python to check the function, so I added `tests/test_gaps.py`. It checks the result on the sample data, confirms the input isn't modified, and uses a small interleaved example to confirm stations never share values. That example includes a station with no temperatures, a row with no station ID, and repeated index labels. You can keep the file or delete it.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
